From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] devices: add display panel for Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro

This one is against gmobile (https://gitlab.gnome.org/World/Phosh/gmobile),
not pmaports. Tested against gmobile 0.7.3.

The POCO X3 Pro has a centred hole-punch camera, and without an entry here Phosh
lays out its top panel as if the screen were a plain rectangle — the clock ends
up directly underneath the camera.

Geometry follows xiaomi,sweet (Redmi Note 10 Pro), which is the same 6.67"
1080x2400 class of device with a centred cutout, with the radius opened up a
little to 28px. Erring large only reserves a few extra pixels; erring small puts
the clock back under the camera.

Verified on the device: with this entry the shell moves the clock clear of the
cutout and nothing is drawn underneath it.

---
 data/devices/display-panels/xiaomi,vayu.json | 13 +++++++++++++
 data/gmobile.gresources.xml                  |  1 +
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/devices/display-panels/xiaomi,vayu.json
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+{
+  "name": "Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro",
+  "x-res": 1080,
+  "y-res": 2400,
+  "corner-radii": [90, 90, 90, 90],
+  "cutouts": [
+    {
+      "name": "front-camera",
+      "path": "M 512,52 a 28,28 0 1,0 56,0 a 28,28 0 1,0 -56,0 Z"
+    }
+  ]
+}
--- a/data/gmobile.gresources.xml
+++ b/data/gmobile.gresources.xml
@@ -33,5 +33,6 @@
     <file preprocess="json-stripblanks">devices/display-panels/xiaomi,onclite.json</file>
     <file preprocess="json-stripblanks">devices/display-panels/xiaomi,lavender.json</file>
     <file preprocess="json-stripblanks">devices/display-panels/xiaomi,sweet.json</file>
+    <file preprocess="json-stripblanks">devices/display-panels/xiaomi,vayu.json</file>
   </gresource>
 </gresources>
